[?2004hroot@n30009:/app# cat docs/README.md
[?2004l# ForgeKit

Internal build automation tool for the C package monorepo.

## Packages

| Name | Type | Version | Dependencies |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| libbase | library | 1.0.0 | (none) |
| libcrypto | library | 1.2.0 | libbase |
| libnet | library | 1.1.0 | libbase |
| libstore | library | 1.3.0 | libbase, libcrypto |
| svc-auth | service | 2.0.1 | libcrypto, libstore |
| svc-gateway | service | 2.1.0 | libnet, libcrypto |
| svc-worker | service | 1.5.0 | libstore, libnet |
| svc-scheduler | service | 1.0.0 | libstore, libnet, libcrypto |

## Usage

```bash
./forge build --all          # build everything in dependency order
./forge build --package NAME # build a specific package and its deps
./forge test --all           # run tests for all packages
./forge list                 # list packages
./forge deps NAME            # show dependency tree
./forge report               # generate build report
./forge config generate ENV  # generate deployment configs
./forge artifact pack NAME   # package a build artifact
./forge clean --all          # remove all build artifacts
```

## Manifest Format

Each package has a `package.forge` file:

```
[package]
name = libbase
version = 1.0.0
type = library

[deps]
deps = dep1,dep2

[build]
command = make
test_command = make test
output = build/libbase.a

[meta]
description = Package description
tags = tag1,tag2
```

## Test Suite

Run the internal test suite:

```bash
bash tests/run_tests.sh
```
